From 0a2c559f050569c236edae6bb68f4fed6f4fdc67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Allen <cma@bitemyapp.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 18:24:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Time frames in SIDESTEP_TRACE_FRAMES, and trace tiles on
 request

Every trace line now starts with the milliseconds since the first, so
the main thread's passes and the render thread's presents line up. A
pass reports its whole main-thread time, with what layout and
viewWillDraw and layer-backed views' canvases took of it, in one line
with the tiles and paints it recorded. A present reports the render
thread's time on the main thread's messages since the last present and
the longest of them, which is where a slow tile's rasterizing shows.

SIDESTEP_TRACE_FRAMES=tiles adds a line for each tile paint: where it
is, whether it was drawn ahead of a scroll, and how many operations and
glyph runs it holds, which is how a view leaving tiles blank shows up.

Signed-off-by: Chris Allen <cma@bitemyapp.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
